      "seed": 2090116822,
      "version": 66,
      "versionNonce": 623828554,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786474504602,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "* Collector per host → bounded local WAL → regional ingest → durable log. \n* From the log, one path writes raw telemetry to Parquet/Iceberg object storage; \nanother performs dedup, enrichment, gap detection, and 30s/5m/1h aggregation into a hot OLAP store. \n* The dashboard query layer auto-selects granularity so three-month trends never scan 1s raw data, \nwhile incident drilldowns retain per-GPU per-second visibility. \n* For Natural Language →SQL, authorization is enforced outside the model: \ngenerate against curated semantic views, parse the AST, inject mandatory tenant/cluster filters,\n reject mutations, estimate cost with EXPLAIN, enforce time/row/CPU limits, run with read-only credentials, and audit every query. \n* Concern: late/duplicate telemetry, cardinality, retention cost, quiet gap detection, schema rollout, backpressure, and making freshness visible.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* Collector per host → bounded local WAL → regional ingest → durable log. \n* From the log, one path writes raw telemetry to Parquet/Iceberg object storage; \nanother performs dedup, enrichment, gap detection, and 30s/5m/1h aggregation into a hot OLAP store. \n* The dashboard query layer auto-selects granularity so three-month trends never scan 1s raw data, \nwhile incident drilldowns retain per-GPU per-second visibility. \n* For Natural Language →SQL, authorization is enforced outside the model: \ngenerate against curated semantic views, parse the AST, inject mandatory tenant/cluster filters,\n reject mutations, estimate cost with EXPLAIN, enforce time/row/CPU limits, run with read-only credentials, and audit every query. \n* Concern: late/duplicate telemetry, cardinality, retention cost, quiet gap detection, schema rollout, backpressure, and making freshness visible.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
